module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.transport_output_field_without_a_native_realization_channel

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundOnRung, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { MechanicallyPreventable, Mitigatable }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

// THE INVALID STATE: a service operation declares a transport output FIELD the native (emitted) realization
// has no channel for. The model then promises a caller a typed arm it can match, and the emission refuses
// the whole entry closure -- the refusal lands on whichever entry first reaches the operation, far from the
// declaration that cannot be lowered. Found while proving the 2026-11-01 native CargoBuild ruling, by
// executing the emission rather than reasoning about it.
data transport_output_field_without_a_native_realization_channel: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "transport_output_field_without_a_native_realization_channel" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead {
    found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
    standing: BelowCeiling {
      current: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
      ceiling: MechanicallyPreventable,
      blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
      trigger_capability: "the capability of judging a declared transport output key against the channels the native realization lowers, at the declaration, instead of at the first entry that happens to reach the operation -- either by modelling an outcome channel in the shell transport, or by refusing the key where it is declared"
    }
  },

  receipts: [
    "**EXECUTED, NOT INFERRED.** A compiler-route entry reaching extdeps.rust.cargo_build_service CargoBuild refused at emit (gunbc compile, 2026-11-02): 'native effect realization refused for entry nefx.cli_probe.v2_cli_main': service extdeps.rust.cargo_build_service CargoBuild has no native realization: operation 'Build' binds no transport: shell transport output key 'outcome' has no modeled channel -- the modeled channels are stdout, stderr, exit_success, success, exists, exit_code, stdout_lines, stderr_truncated, stderr_total_bytes and stderr_retained_bytes'. The sentence is owned by the v1.compiler.emit symbol shell_emission_refusal_fact -- cited by symbol, because its position in that module moves with any edit above it. The operation had declared 'outcome: ShellOutcome' beside exit_code/stdout/stderr, exactly as extdeps.transports.shell describes the field.",

    "**THE TWO HALVES DISAGREE, AND THAT IS THE CLASS.** The interpreter models the field: the v1.stage0 v1_interpreter host both documents that ShellSpawnRefused is returned as a VALUE so the evaluation continues, and renders the advice a reader follows -- 'declare an extdeps.transports.shell ShellOutcome output field to receive this as ShellSpawnRefused'. The quoted diagnostic text is the identifier here: that host is one large evaluation body, so a line pointer into it is stale the moment anything above it moves. The emitter has no channel for it. So the same declaration is legal, useful and unbuildable at once, and the advice the interpreter gives leads straight into the emission refusal.",

    "**THE POPULATION THAT ALREADY CARRIES IT, BY GREP, NOT HYPOTHESIS.** Read at 5b0b26d9b399 (2026-11-02) with: git grep -l 'outcome: ShellOutcome' 5b0b26d9b399 -- dag (population: the whole of dag/). Five corpus modules declare the field: extdeps.shell.exec (service Exec, dag/extdeps/shell/exec.dag:199), extdeps.systemd.systemctl (service Systemctl, dag/extdeps/systemd/systemctl.dag:657, :675, :828), extdeps.github.ci_runner, extdeps.github.organizations and gunbc.compute.work_provider_local. None is reachable from an admitted native entry today -- the compiler route's declared set names extdeps.filesystem.filesystem_io Filesystem and extdeps.rust.cargo_build_service CargoBuild, the claim route names extdeps.docker.cli_service DockerCli -- so the gap is latent, and it fires the first time one of these operations is lowered for a native entry. The class does not care which transport: the keys it accepts are transport-specific lists, and this row names the shell one because that is the one measured.",

    "**RUNG FOUND AT: Mitigatable.** Today the guard is the emission refusal itself, which is loud and typed and stops the build -- no plausible output is fabricated. It is not yet MechanicallyPreventable because the refusal is located at the ENTRY, not at the declaration: an author adding an output field to a shared service sees a failure in an unrelated closure, and the five existing declarations were never judged at all.",

    "**DISSOLUTION CONDITION, CONCRETE.** The row dissolves when either (a) the shell transport models an outcome channel, and an executed control shows a spawn refusal arriving as ShellSpawnRefused DATA on a native route instead of refusing the compile, or (b) the checker judges every declared transport output key against that transport's channel list at the declaration site, and an executed witness shows a service declaring an unlowerable key refused there with the key named. H1 takes neither option: it drops the field from the one operation it owns and records the refusal above, rather than leaving a declaration that only ever refuses downstream.",

    "**NAMED OWNER.** The native-backend lane (manager clever-crane-830, work item adhoc-b3b5b3ae-af9), which owns the native realization and is where the refusal was measured.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.transports.shell", decl_name: "ShellOutcome"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.rust.cargo_build_service", decl_name: "CargoBuild"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.shell.exec", decl_name: "Exec"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.systemd.systemctl", decl_name: "Systemctl"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "std.compiler_entry", decl_name: "native_compiler_route_denominator"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "std.compiler_entry", decl_name: "native_claim_route_denominator"),
  ],
}
